diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..e14ed24 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,38 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP
+
+The shared layout exposes browser tools through `use-webmcp-tool`, which checks
+for `document.modelContext` and unregisters tools with an AbortSignal when its
+React island unmounts during Astro navigation. Ordinary controls continue to
+work when WebMCP is unavailable. Native agent discovery requires a browser with
+WebMCP enabled in a secure context; no MCP server or transport is needed.
+
+| Tool | Availability | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `open_search` | All pages using the shared layout | Opens and loads the search form |
+| `search_articles` | Search flyout open | Matches titles and summaries; returns article details and links |
+| `open_reading_list` | Shared layout | Loads articles and saved entries, then opens the reading-list form |
+| `toggle_reading_list` | Reading-list flyout open | Saves an article, or removes it if saved; returns updated saved slugs |
+| `list_articles` | Shared layout | Article catalogue with summaries and links |
+| `get_article_details` | Shared layout | Summary and link for a validated article slug |
+| `get_reading_list` | Shared layout | Saved slugs with matching article details and links |
+| `read_current_article` | Article pages | Displayed headline, summary, article body, and current URL |
+
+Search and reading-list forms use `toolname`, `tooldescription`,
+`toolparamdescription`, named native controls, and `toolautosubmit` for these
+read-only or reversible operations. Their submit handlers read `FormData` so
+agent-populated values use the same behavior as manual submissions. For agent
+submissions, the native submit event's `respondWith()` receives the result after
+UI updates. Errors are returned as structured payloads. Form activation and
+submission get native WebMCP outline styles.
+
+Article utilities share base-path-aware client requests with the UI. Network
+utility tools forward the execution AbortSignal, and reading-list updates notify
+all mounted bookmark controls. Reading lists continue to use the existing
+session-backed API. The intentionally failing network demonstrations embedded
+in article content remain as DevTools exercises.
+
+Validation: `pnpm run build`. This builds the app without starting a server.
